#description Practice game 91, 2026-07-12. Reconstructed (Opus) from Jesse's scoresheet and final board photo; replaces an earlier reconstruction.
#note Board-true reconstruction verified by an exact-score joint solve and a clean 100/100 tile-bag audit. Jesse moved first and OPENED WITH AN EXCHANGE of L and W (scoresheet "x2"; the kept tiles AINRT + a drawn Q enabled QAT next turn) - so Jesse is player1 here. Two places differ from the paper record. (1) James's going-out play is VEE at 14H (the third E sits on the J14 triple-letter square; it crosses REV down column H and AME down column I), whose board-true value is 19, not the 13 written at the table - James under-scored it by 6. (VEE at 14G, which would score 23, is impossible: it forms the phony crossword EHV, and the R-overdraw in the tile bag rules out reading the word as VER.) (2) Jesse's scoresheet carries an unexplained final "+6" (paper total 406) with no word attached; with the board full at 100 tiles and Jesse holding a single leftover D, no placement can add 6, so it is a paper tally slip and Jesse's true final is 400. James goes out; Jesse's leftover D (2 pts) gives James +4. Net board-true result: Jesse 400, James 444 (paper had 406-438; a prior reconstruction had 400-448 from mis-placing VEE at 14G). Racks are declared as played tiles only (partial) mid-game, with true full racks in the endgame, as the Woogles importer requires.
